data pre_existing_hand_retained_registration_backfill_note: String = "Five files were already committed as declared hand-retained Rust oracles (each self-documents its own authority + dissolve-on trigger: cssl_seed_linked_closure_assembly cites tools.self_host_curated_seed_linked_harness; required_regen_host realizes v2.workflow.required_regen; v2_compiler_compile / v2_compiler_program_assembly / v2_compiler_source_authority are Wave 2 Gate-A-flip oracles, same shape as the v2_compiler_resolve/tokenize/infer rows already registered above) but were missing rows here, so required_regen_host's compile_stage0()-population comparison correctly reported them as committed_not_emitted. Backfilled during the #8428 regen-survivability fix (gunbc issue: main cannot survive a clean regen) — this population mismatch was pre-existing and unrelated to #8428 itself, but required_regen_host hard-refuses on any mismatch, so it blocked verifying the #8428 fix end-to-end. All five carry has_pub_mod: false, verified against lib.rs (zero pub-mod lines for any of the five) rather than assumed: cssl_seed_linked_closure_assembly is #[path]-wired inside bin/cssl_assemble.rs, required_regen_host is #[path]-wired inside cli_run.rs, and v2_compiler_compile / v2_compiler_program_assembly / v2_compiler_source_authority are Gate-A curated seed-linked (CSSL) oracles compiled standalone by tools.self_host_curated_seed_linked_harness for each frontier row's behavioral-transport witness (dag/gunbc/instruments/self_host_module_behavioral_transport_roster.dag) — never part of the stage0 crate's own mod tree at all."

data data_initializer_identity_seed_retained_note: String = "SeedRetained hand-Rust for resolved data-initializer projection marshaling (decl_facts initializer identity lane, PR #7924). Reason: marshal requires InterpContext typechecked subjects, inferred Node stamps, and owning type-item lookup not yet modeled in .dag. Migration trigger: v2.std.data_initializer_identity projection carriers self-emit and coproduct_reflection routes through the modeled marshal surface; then this module deletes with its SeedRetainedIntrinsicRegistration row. THAT SCHEMA HAS LANDED (2026-08-24): v2.compiler.self_host.seed_retention_frontier carries one row per retained seed file with a cause and a reason, and this file's row there cites this note as its authority rather than restating it. This note therefore stops being a scaffold standing in for a missing field and becomes the reason the field points at; it dissolves with the module, not with the schema."

